so good afternoon ladies and gentlemen  and most warmly welcome to this press  conference of prime minister of finland  and president of the european commission  and the subject of this press conference  is finland's recovery and resilience  plan  we start with the remarks with prime  minister please  thank you so much it's been a great  pleasure to welcome the president of the  commission ursula vandalian to finland  we have a very useful discussion with  her this afternoon  we exchanged views on number of topical  issues  uh concerning europe a major focus of  discussion was how we can best work  towards screen and digital  transformation  in europe  finland has ambitious national goals in  terms of reaching climate neutrality and  boosting digital economy  and accordingly we want the eu to become  the world's most competitive and  socially inclusive climate neutral  economy  we discussed with ursula various aspects  of the fit455 legislative package that  the commission issued  last summer with the goal to cut  greenhouse gas emissions by at least 55  percent  by 2030.  finland supports rapid progress in  negotiations on the package the level of  ambition has to be maintained we  consider emissions trading to be  the main policy measure for achieving  the target  we also exchange views with ursula on  forestry and use new forest strategy  finland's approach towards forests and  forestry is a holistic one  we want to take into account  environmental economic and social  dimensions of sustainability and  recognize the overall potential of  forest and the forest sector  we also discussed autotopical issues  such as the need to move forward in  european defense cooperation  use recovery package is a key tool to  boost digital and korean transition  across the union  as you know major context of this visit  to helsinki is to getting insight into  finland's national recovery plan our  visit here in vtt serves to illustrate  one focus of finland's national recovery  plan  our recovery plan recognizes quantum  computing as one of  as one key aspect of technological  competitiveness in the future  we have just now had an opportunity to  learn more about bt's work to build  finland's first quantum computer  it is a good example on how they use  recovery package can support investment  to advance new technologies  investments in new technologies are  indeed essential to ensure not only the  recovery of our economies but at the  same time in the long term to renewal  our economies  i would like now to give the floor to  the president of the commission ursula  the floor is yours thank you very much  prime minister diazana thank you very  much for  the warm welcome you gave me and my  delegation today  and i would  very much thank you for the fascinating  visit here at vtt the  technical research center  um finland's first quantum computer i've  learned a lot today so that was really  informative  and i think  this is a perfect example for farsighted  investment here in finland we heard a  lot about it  and indeed we need to strengthen  europe's technological leadership  and thus create quality jobs that are  needed  and that is the spirit in which we  design next generation eu  the 800 billion  recovery fund  it is much more than simple recovery  we are reshaping our continent for  decades to come  we're making the green deal  a reality and we are also accelerating  digitalization in an unprecedented  manner  so i'm happy to announce that today  the euro european commission has decided  to give its green light  to finland's recovery and resilience  plan  this follows a thorough assessment and  an excellent cooperation  between our teams and i really want to  thank the sunnah for this excellent  cooperation it is outstanding we have  the comparison so thank you very much  for that  the plan includes reforms and investment  it will further accelerate finland's  outstanding  green and digital transitions  and i must say we applaud finland's  ambitious objective to be carbon neutral  by 2035 already  your recovery and resilience plan  will provide an important boost  to this important  goal  so if i look into the plan half of the  plan the finland's plan  is devoted to the green transition to  green projects 50  this is more than it would have been  necessary so you're overshooting  the necessary requirements and this is  outstanding  it includes spot-on measures  in each of the most polluting sectors  such as energy industry  transport and housing  it will invest in just to give a few  examples  low carbon hydrogen  in clean energy technologies  it will finance green transport  and very important roll out charging  points along the roads  for cars  it will for example replace oil boilers  with low or zero carbon heating system  so that is investing in the european  green deal at its best  the second objective we have in next  generation eu is the digital  and finland is already a leader in the  digital transition in the european union  and in the world  so now you devote 27  of the plan to support the digital  objectives  and this  for sure will help finland to sustain  its leading position  the plan will support research in 6g  artificial intelligence microelectronics  high-speed connectivity  and very pleased about your plan to  connect the rural areas that will  benefit from the investment in the  digital connectivity and digital rail  services for example  i also like very much that the plan will  help the public sector  to go more digital this is always needed  and it will equip finnish workers with  digital skills  they need to be ready for the future  but next generation u is not only about  investments the finished plan also  contains a range of crucial reforms  the plan anchors the  2035 carbon neutrality  goal into finnish law  the plan will phase out the use of coal  and make finland's tax policy greener  in other words there too this plan will  strengthen finland's position as green  front runner in the european union  and last but not least it is also very  good that your plan aims to strengthen  the national health system  we have learned our lessons from the  pandemic and we know how important it is  to invest in the healthcare sector so to  upgrade existing medical facilities  you will invest in the development of  ehealth  your plan will increase the number of  higher education  study places  and of course also address the shortage  of health workers  in the medium term  because investing in our future is  investing in our health and in the  health of the planet  so i have the pleasure to hand over now  the envelope that gives green light to  the finnish clan  thank you very much thank you  thank you so much  and we have time ursula a few questions  and we start with the wiley and kindly  represent yourself and your media before  making the question  from wiley  we have learned about a new data leak  pandora's papers revealing that  thousands of people are still using  taking advantage of tax havens even the  high-ranking politicians what is your  assessment about the situation and is  there something that eu or member states  could do in order to avoid  tax avoidance thank you  yes so  tax evasion and aggressive tax planning  is completely unacceptable  and  we have in the european union some of  the highest tax transparency standards  in the world  but as we see it's not enough more work  is needed  and that's why we will come forward with  a proposal on the misuse of shell  companies  for tax purposes and this will be done  till the end of the year so we'll come  with an answer to the obvious problems  that are still out there  well of course uh tax avoidance is a  serious problem and i want to thank the  journalists  that  came this avoidance's delight so thanks  to those journalists and i'm very happy  that the commission is also doing its  best  to to make sure that these kind of  elements are being  ripped out of our system so so we are  taking this issue very seriously and we  are working with the commission and with  the member states to make sure that that  these kind of problems don't occur in  the future anymore  good afternoon one question to the  president  of the european commission is it  possible that the recovery and  resilience plan or a similar program  will be re-implemented in the future  whether  it is  one-off  i think that  many ordinary citizens still have doubts  about this in finland thank you very  much yes thank you very much um so  we had and have an unprecedented crisis  with the pandemic  and the lockdowns and the paralyzing of  our economy and thus this unprecedented  crisis needed an unprecedented answer  but the  one off is built in  if i may say so  so therefore this is in itself an agreed  system  what we will focus now on is delivery  and implementation this is the 21st  um recovering resilience plan so we're  almost done with designing the plans and  they are designed by the member states  with the objectives we agree on the  european union this is the green deal it  is digitalization its resilience and now  it's a lot about implementation  implementation implementation we have  the milestones the targets and this will  bring the european union and the single  market forward  another question to the president of  commission uh economy is now forecast to  grow by uh 4.8  this year and 4.5 percent next year in  the eu and  euro area  why do we need to stimulate the growth  more with this massive package  why the economy is growing very strongly  in the eu and europe area why do we need  this massive  massive stimulus package yes because  what we've seen with of course the  economy is growing because it has been  shrinking so much  so if you lower the level  where you start the  jump forward is a big one but we've lost  a lot of economic power over the  pandemic that's the one point the second  point is  as you know now reshaping the world the  whole world has to get back into its  economy we see  that  a lot of supply chains have been cut  a lot of businesses have gone out of  business have gone bust  so what we do now is we invest  in a way that with the recovery we  always have also have the leap forward  into modernization of our economy and  therefore we were very strict  that the agreed amount of investment has  to go as i said in the european green  deal  37 of the whole package goes straight  into the european green deal and green  projects so important to invest in this  transition 20 at least have to go into  the digital and you see here in finland  finland has even invested more in the  green and even invested more in the  digital  and a certain portion has to go into the  resilience which is improving our single  market  so we use the time starting low  in the crisis to really jump forward and  modernize and to be come out stronger  out of the crisis then we went into the  crisis  i i agree with ursula it's not only  about financial tool it's actually the  way we build our economies from the  bottom up so we are now transforming our  economies  to the more green more digital so it's  much more than just the stimulus package  it's to do with our our basic economies  and and to build our societies in a new  way  can i perhaps add an example i learned  so much here with quantum computing also  what you invest this is just the right  thing to do  because today  we are defining whether we're going to  be  world leaders or at least competitive in  the quantum computing age  or whether we're going to lag behind  and we see that a lot of investment is  needed to modernize  the same as for example the lack of  semiconductors we see at the moment  being so we want to create an ecosystem  that really works to  get us more independent of the pro in  the production of semiconductors because  we know it's desperately needed for our  economy  we have sectors where the production is  slowed down because of lack of  semiconductors  so this modernizing is crucial to be  competitive also in 10 years and in 20  years  female is one of the eight member states  that have signed a letter critical to  loosening the eu rules on deficit and  public debt did you discuss the issue  today and what are your opinions on  reforming the fiscal rules including the  stability and growth pact thank you yeah  the stability and growth pact important  will be in the fall  to have a common diagnosis  what is the situation of the economy  right now what is the fiscal um  what are the fiscal circumstances we  have right now and for me it's very  important really to listen to all and to  find a consensus that we build within  the european union so it's time now for  the diagnosis  are of course  waiting the commission's proposals  on this finland  once  to make sure that the european economy  in every member states is a sustainable  path and that's why we have sent the  letter to commission but now we're  waiting for the commercial proposals and  we are always open to discuss but still  still we need to make sure that our  economies are are in the solid ground in  the future thank you very much prime  minister thank you very much president  of the commission thank you everyone and  have a very nice evening

